From 7e7f8a2dd290508c9cb98d7cf3f533a7c27fb4a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] Meter: a header button for each plugin overlay

A plugin that names an overlay in its manifest (ui.overlay: the Map's
overlay, the Inventory's limits) gets a button of its own in the meter's
header, before the plugins button: it shows or hides that overlay alone,
the plugin window staying as it is, and is gold while the overlay shows.
The plugin hears "overlay" and opens or closes its widget, as its own
switch does. With the plugins turned off by the plugins button, the
overlay asked for shows on its own; the plugins button hides or shows
them all again.

A widget moved by its plugin (a2.widgets.place) moves on KDE's native
Wayland too, where no app may move a window: it goes and comes back, and
KWin puts it at the place the meter keeps; a2.widgets.where says the
place KWin last reported there.
